// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// Docs-accuracy pass, post bench #11 (bonding system + mixed-element
// benches). Two kinds of fix bundled together:
//
// 1. docs/architecture.md and docs/getting-started.md described the
//    PRE-refactor design (C#-owned NativeArray<AtomData> passed into Rust
//    by pointer, boot-time ChemDataLoader) -- superseded by the current
//    Rust-owns-the-atom-array design (chem_context_create/chem_spawn_atom/
//    chem_despawn_atom, AtomHandle) since before bench #11, but never
//    updated to match. Rewritten to reflect the real FFI surface, real
//    units (eV / fs / Angstrom, not kcal/mol / ps), the new bonding
//    system, and current element coverage (5 elements: H, He, Li, Be, B --
//    cross-checked clean against DixScript-Rust's elements_database.mdix
//    and core/physics.mdix's formulas, no discrepancies found).
// 2. Two small bugs caught during that pass, fixed inline rather than
//    filed separately since they're one-line each:
//      - chemistry_core/Cargo.toml's dependency comment claimed a Rust
//        1.80+ floor. Real floor is 1.83+ -- mid-math's sse2 module uses
//        `f32::from_bits` in a const context (const-stable since 1.83),
//        compiled unconditionally on x86/x86_64 regardless of the
//        force-scalar feature (verified: force-scalar does NOT route
//        around it). CI has never caught this because
//        dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable always installs newest, not the
//        documented floor.
//      - lib.rs's chem_step doc comment said "seconds"; dt is actually
//        femtoseconds (matches simulation::step's own comment and what
//        AMU_TO_EFF_MASS requires dimensionally). Fixed at both the
//        function doc and the module-level C# usage example, since that's
//        the exact snippet Runtime/Core would get written against next.
//
// Root README.md's [[project_name]]/[[description]] template placeholders
// also filled in while touching that file, plus a Status section so it
// stops underselling how far chemistry_core already is relative to the
// still-scaffold-only Unity package side.
//
// packages/com.midmanstudio.alembic/Documentation~/index.md gets one small
// touch -- its pipeline diagram now says "bonding" instead of "SIMD" in
// the chemistry_core column (SIMD is still in the tree behind a feature
// flag, but bonding is the more load-bearing fact to put in a one-line
// summary now). Left that file's chemistry-data-ownership claim alone --
// whether Unity loads raw physics constants via com.midmanstudio.mdix at
// runtime, vs. Rust keeping its own hand-synced copy the way it does
// today, reads like an open architecture question rather than a verified
// bug, so not overriding it here.
//
// Not bundled here, flagged instead: .github/workflows/rust-rust-ci.yml's
// own `paths:` trigger says `.github/workflows/rust-ci.yml` -- filename on
// disk doesn't match, so edits to that workflow file won't retrigger it.
// Content-identical rename, no line changes needed -- easiest done by hand
// via GitHub's edit-then-rename-at-top UI rather than shipping a
// duplicate .yml through this pipeline for a pure rename.
//
// ROOT_README.md -> README.md via overrides:: below, same reasoning as
// this repo's last replacements batch: a flat "README.md" at this
// archive's top level would basename-search the whole repo and hit an
// ambiguous-match error now that there are two (this one, and
// packages/com.midmanstudio.alembic/README.md). Everything else nested,
// resolves directly.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  features   -> "data,quickfuncs"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  ~target<object>(name, path) { return { name = name, path = path } }
)

@DATA(
  target_root = "."

  overrides::
    target("ROOT_README.md", "README.md")
)
